# 10 Results: RCM error budget and variance decomposition

Generated by `analysis.py` from folder 09's per-run results plus bags, META tool geometry and both kinematic models. mm rms unless stated. Budget in quadrature: total² = latch² + fitted²; fitted² = controller² + kinematic² + chain².

**Tracker floor on the RCM metric** (`V9b/NDIStaticFloor`, arm still, 31 s, 1849 samples): 0.085 mm rms, p95 0.079 mm, about a point on the mean shaft. The recorder's 0.73 mm for this run is distance to an older latched point (a constant offset, not noise).

## Budget per set and condition (median over replays)

| Set | day · kinematics | total | controller | latch offset | rest (kinematics + measurement chain) | model difference, same tool (INVALID, see note) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| RCM only | 2026-10-26 · nominal | 0.43 | 0.06 | 0.22 | 0.36 | 0.65 |
| RCM only | 2026-11-03 · calibrated | 0.47 | 0.06 | 0.30 | 0.37 | 0.62 |
| RCM only | 2026-11-06 · calibrated | 0.45 | 0.06 | 0.05 | 0.45 | 0.62 |
| Whole run | 2026-10-26 · nominal | 0.90 | 0.08 | 0.45 | 0.78 | 0.66 |
| Whole run | 2026-11-03 · calibrated | 1.23 | 0.08 | 0.96 | 0.77 | 0.63 |
| Whole run | 2026-11-06 · calibrated | 0.91 | 0.08 | 0.66 | 0.62 | 0.64 |
| Fast checking | 2026-10-26 · nominal | 1.70 | 0.23 | 1.37 | 0.98 | 0.97 |
| Fast checking | 2026-11-03 · calibrated | 1.21 | 0.25 | 1.00 | 0.63 | 0.95 |
| Fast checking | 2026-11-06 · calibrated | 1.80 | 0.25 | 1.61 | 0.78 | 0.96 |
| Slow checking | 2026-10-26 · nominal | 2.87 | 0.05 | 2.64 | 1.13 | 0.59 |
| Slow checking | 2026-11-03 · calibrated | 1.32 | 0.05 | 1.16 | 0.63 | 0.60 |
| Slow checking | 2026-11-06 · calibrated | 1.90 | 0.05 | 1.69 | 0.85 | 0.60 |

**Note: the kinematic term is not separated here.** Pushing the same tool geometry through the nominal and the calibrated model gives a "model difference" of 0.6–1.0 mm, larger than the *total* measured error on some runs (e.g. RCM only, 10-26), which is impossible for a real error component. The tool (hand–eye) calibration was itself fitted through one model, so swapping the model without refitting the tool creates an artificial difference. A valid kinematic term needs the tool refitted per model from the raw hand–eye recordings (`src/ndi_tracking/calibrations/raw/robot_tcp_*.npz`, joints recovered by IK), as planned in ANALYSIS.md; until then kinematics and the measurement chain are reported together as "rest".

## Variance decomposition of log(NDI rms), calibrated days (11-03 and 11-06)

54 runs. Partial η² per factor (type II, OLS on log rms), 95 % bootstrap interval over replays within cells.

| Factor | partial η² | 95 % interval |
|---|---|---|
| set | 0.975 | 0.972–0.984 |
| day | 0.126 | 0.075–0.263 |
| mode | 0.222 | 0.185–0.356 |
| set:day | 0.762 | 0.732–0.833 |

## Summary

- Controller's own error 0.05–0.26 mm; tracker floor 0.085 mm.
- Kinematic term: not separated (see note); E0's 0.1–0.35 mm is untested here.
- Latch offset: median 0.96 mm, max 2.69 mm.

## Prior claims checked

- "kinematics explain only 0.1–0.35 mm (E0)": see the kinematic and counterfactual columns.
- "a ~2.5 mm latch-pose offset dominates SlowChecking (10-26)": see the latch column.
- "trajectory and camera dominate, mode is negligible": see the η² table.

